        "`cball_to_cinterval(b)`: converts a complex ball `list(re, im, rad)` to a rectangular interval `list(re_lo, re_hi, im_lo, im_hi)`. Converts this disk into an enclosing rectangular [`Cball`].",
        "`cdf(d, x)`: cumulative distribution function `P(X <= x)` of distribution `d` at point `x`. The point shares the distribution's dimension and the probability is dimensionless. Floating normal, lognormal, exponential, Weibull, and Cauchy calls use tail-stable evaluation.",
        "`cdt_2d(points, segments)`: the constrained Delaunay triangulation of `points` that keeps every `list(i, j)` segment as an edge. Delaunay triangulation of `points` with the given segments forced in. Each `(u, v)` in `segments` becomes a chain of constrained edges in the returned triangulation: any segment passing through existing collinear vertices is automatically split at those vertices before enforcement. # Errors Returns `Err` when the points are invalid, when a segment index is out of range, when a segment joins a vertex to itself, or when two segments cross transversely (in which case [`constrained_delaunay_2d_mesh`] should be used so the intersection Steiner points can be returned).",
        "`ceil(x)`: smallest integer greater than or equal to `x`.",
