        "`central_binomial(n)`: central binomial coefficient `C(2n, n)`.",
        "`central_moment_of(d, k)`: `k`-th central moment `E[(X - E[X])^k]` of distribution `d`.",
        "`centripetal_acceleration(v, r)`: centripetal acceleration magnitude `v^2 / r` for speed `v` and radius `r`.",
        "`cfrac(x)`: continued fraction expansion `[a0, a1, ...]` of rational or quadratic-irrational `x`.",
        "`chain(terms)`: formal linear combination `list(list(mult, cell), ...)` of oriented cells.",
        "`chain_autocorrelation(chain, max_lag)`: the sample autocorrelation of `chain` for lags `0..=max_lag`. Sample autocorrelation of `chain` at lags `0..=max_lag`. The estimate uses the usual biased denominator, the full sum of squared deviations from the mean, so the sequence is positive semidefinite. Lag 0 is always 1. Entries that cannot be estimated \u2014 a chain with fewer than two draws, a lag of at least the chain length, or a constant chain \u2014 are `NaN`.",
        "Computes the `k`-th Adams operation `g -> chi(g^k)` on class function `chi` of finite group `G`.",
        "Computes the alternating (exterior) square `(chi(g)^2 - chi(g^2)) / 2` of class function `chi` on finite group `G`.",
        "Computes the complex conjugate `conj(chi)` of class function `chi` on finite group `G`.",
        "Decomposes class function `chi` into multiplicities of the irreducible characters of finite group `G`.",
        "Computes the character inner product `(1/|G|) * sum_{g in G} chi(g) * conj(psi(g))` for class functions `chi` and `psi`.",
        "Returns `true` if class function `chi` of finite group `G` has `<chi, chi> = 1`.",
