        "`cofactors(A)`: cofactor matrix of square matrix `A`.",
        "`coherence(x, y, window, hop, sample_rate)`: one-sided magnitude-squared Welch coherence. Bins with zero power have zero coherence. Estimates one-sided cross-spectral density and magnitude-squared coherence. Applies the same complete-frame Welch convention as [`welch_psd`] to both inputs. For the Fourier bins `X` and `Y`, it averages `conj(X) * Y` across frames to obtain the cross-spectral density `Pxy`, and computes `abs(Pxy)^2 / (Pxx * Pyy)`. Auto-spectra and cross-spectra share the same window energy and one-sided scaling. # Errors Returns an error on unequal lengths or on the invalid input domains described by [`welch_psd`].",
        "`collect(expr, var)`: groups terms of `expr` by powers of `var`.",
        "`colspace(A)`: basis of the column space of matrix `A`.",
