        "`fresnel_c_complex(re, im)`: `list(re, im)` of the complex Fresnel cosine integral `C(re + i*im)`. `(S(z), C(z))` for a complex argument `z = re + i\u00b7im`, returned as `((S.re, S.im), (C.re, C.im))`. With `a = \u221a\u03c0/2`, `E\u2081 = erf(a (1-i) z)`, `E\u2082 = erf(a (1+i) z)`: `C(z) = (1+i)/4 \u00b7 E\u2081 + (1-i)/4 \u00b7 E\u2082`, `S(z) = (1-i)/4 \u00b7 E\u2081 + (1+i)/4 \u00b7 E\u2082`. Real arguments take the real kernels, so they keep full accuracy.",
        "`fresnel_s_complex(re, im)`: `list(re, im)` of the complex Fresnel sine integral `S(re + i*im)`. `(S(z), C(z))` for a complex argument `z = re + i\u00b7im`, returned as `((S.re, S.im), (C.re, C.im))`. With `a = \u221a\u03c0/2`, `E\u2081 = erf(a (1-i) z)`, `E\u2082 = erf(a (1+i) z)`: `C(z) = (1+i)/4 \u00b7 E\u2081 + (1-i)/4 \u00b7 E\u2082`, `S(z) = (1-i)/4 \u00b7 E\u2081 + (1+i)/4 \u00b7 E\u2082`. Real arguments take the real kernels, so they keep full accuracy.",
