        "Actual native DG method with explicit geometry/time and per-component physical references; normalized states, separate flux units and coherent compiled callbacks preserve mixed Euler dimensions. Native algorithm and limiter identity are retained; shapes, work and parent lifetimes are checked.",
        "Prepares periodic scalar DG advection on a one-dimensional mesh at a fixed measured velocity. The plan retains the nodal differentiation and surface weights. Prepares the Legendre\u2013Gauss\u2013Lobatto operator for a fixed mesh and velocity. # Errors Returns an error for invalid one-dimensional geometry, degree, velocity or work size.",
        "Actual native DG method with explicit geometry/time and per-component physical references; normalized states, separate flux units and coherent compiled callbacks preserve mixed Euler dimensions. Native algorithm and limiter identity are retained; shapes, work and parent lifetimes are checked. Advance periodic scalar DG advection from its nodal state by one SSPRK3 step. The caller controls the physical step and must respect the DG CFL limit; this restart interface reuses the existing DG volume/surface operator. # Errors Invalid mesh/state/time, a non-finite speed, or a step above the DG CFL limit.",
        "Actual native DG method with explicit geometry/time and per-component physical references; normalized states, separate flux units and coherent compiled callbacks preserve mixed Euler dimensions. Native algorithm and limiter identity are retained; shapes, work and parent lifetimes are checked. Advance periodic scalar DG advection in one or two dimensions by SSPRK3. # Errors Invalid mesh, velocity/state dimensions, time controls, or multidimensional CFL.",
        "Advances the prepared periodic DG plan by one positive measured time interval within its CFL bound. The input and output are element-major nodal vectors with the mesh field dimension. Advances a nodal state by one SSPRK3 step and returns the new state. # Errors Returns the same validation and numerical errors as [`Self::step_into`].",
