        "Native exact algebraic topology with session-owned, kind/version checked complex, chain and presentation handles. Complex inputs/exports use CSR offsets/indices. Handles are invalid in other sessions and after release; all objects own their data. Finite construction bounds: 4096 simplices, 12 vertices per simplex, 65536 face/storage words, 256 generators per chain group and 128 x 128 exact matrix elimination. Presentation simplification accepts sixteen generators and 256 input word coefficients with the native 4000-word intermediate limit; product frontiers are bounded to 1048576 coefficient slots. Cubical chains accept 64 pixels; direct cubical Betti accepts 4096. Filtrations carry a canonical value_unit witness verified against stored radius dimensions. Bars use explicit essential flags and zero death placeholders; bottleneck inputs are births/deaths/essential records and unequal essential counts give positive infinity. Products return None on their native simplex limit; malformed inputs and adapter budget exhaustion are errors. Pure source algorithms are invoked in RSSN kernels; opaque payloads contain only session handles, never serialized pointers. Checks the Mayer-Vietoris sequence of `A \u222a B` at the level of ranks. the Euler characteristics add up, and there are nonnegative ranks of the connecting maps that make every stretch of the long exact sequence exact. Returns the ranks of the connecting maps `H_k(A \u222a B) -> H_{k-1}(A \u2229 B)` for `k = 1 ..` when the check passes.",
        "Native exact algebraic topology with session-owned, kind/version checked complex, chain and presentation handles. Complex inputs/exports use CSR offsets/indices. Handles are invalid in other sessions and after release; all objects own their data. Finite construction bounds: 4096 simplices, 12 vertices per simplex, 65536 face/storage words, 256 generators per chain group and 128 x 128 exact matrix elimination. Presentation simplification accepts sixteen generators and 256 input word coefficients with the native 4000-word intermediate limit; product frontiers are bounded to 1048576 coefficient slots. Cubical chains accept 64 pixels; direct cubical Betti accepts 4096. Filtrations carry a canonical value_unit witness verified against stored radius dimensions. Bars use explicit essential flags and zero death placeholders; bottleneck inputs are births/deaths/essential records and unequal essential counts give positive infinity. Products return None on their native simplex limit; malformed inputs and adapter budget exhaustion are errors. Pure source algorithms are invoked in RSSN kernels; opaque payloads contain only session handles, never serialized pointers. Persistent homology over `Z/2` of a filtered complex. The input is `(value, simplex)` pairs (any order; every face of a simplex must be present with a value no larger). Bars of dimension up to `max_dim` with positive length are returned, sorted by dimension, birth, death. This is the standard algorithm: the columns of the boundary matrix, ordered by (value, dimension, lexicographic), are reduced from left to right until their lowest ones are distinct.",
        "Native exact algebraic topology with session-owned, kind/version checked complex, chain and presentation handles. Complex inputs/exports use CSR offsets/indices. Handles are invalid in other sessions and after release; all objects own their data. Finite construction bounds: 4096 simplices, 12 vertices per simplex, 65536 face/storage words, 256 generators per chain group and 128 x 128 exact matrix elimination. Presentation simplification accepts sixteen generators and 256 input word coefficients with the native 4000-word intermediate limit; product frontiers are bounded to 1048576 coefficient slots. Cubical chains accept 64 pixels; direct cubical Betti accepts 4096. Filtrations carry a canonical value_unit witness verified against stored radius dimensions. Bars use explicit essential flags and zero death placeholders; bottleneck inputs are births/deaths/essential records and unequal essential counts give positive infinity. Products return None on their native simplex limit; malformed inputs and adapter budget exhaustion are errors. Pure source algorithms are invoked in RSSN kernels; opaque payloads contain only session handles, never serialized pointers. The edge-path presentation of the fundamental group of the component of the smallest vertex: the generators are the edges outside a spanning tree, the relators the boundaries of the triangles.",
