        "Portable native approximation model with independent coordinate and ordinate dimensions. Every query checks kind/version, defining data lengths, finite data, monotone grids where required, interval and allocation budgets. Derivatives restore ordinate/coordinate powers; integrals restore their product. Model values contain only defining data and no process-local references. Derivative of order 1, 2 or 3 at `x` (order 0 is the value).",
        "Portable native approximation model with independent coordinate and ordinate dimensions. Every query checks kind/version, defining data lengths, finite data, monotone grids where required, interval and allocation budgets. Derivatives restore ordinate/coordinate powers; integrals restore their product. Model values contain only defining data and no process-local references. Derivative of order 1, 2 or 3 at `x` (order 0 is the value).",
        "Portable native approximation model with independent coordinate and ordinate dimensions. Every query checks kind/version, defining data lengths, finite data, monotone grids where required, interval and allocation budgets. Derivatives restore ordinate/coordinate powers; integrals restore their product. Model values contain only defining data and no process-local references. Spline value at `x` (extrapolates with the end cubics).",
        "Portable native approximation model with independent coordinate and ordinate dimensions. Every query checks kind/version, defining data lengths, finite data, monotone grids where required, interval and allocation budgets. Derivatives restore ordinate/coordinate powers; integrals restore their product. Model values contain only defining data and no process-local references. Exact integral of the spline over `[lo, hi]`.",
        "Portable native approximation model with independent coordinate and ordinate dimensions. Every query checks kind/version, defining data lengths, finite data, monotone grids where required, interval and allocation budgets. Derivatives restore ordinate/coordinate powers; integrals restore their product. Model values contain only defining data and no process-local references. Builds an interpolating spline through `(x, y)`. # Errors [`ApproxError::Invalid`] for fewer than 3 points (4 for not-a-knot) non-increasing abscissae, or non-finite data or clamped derivatives; [`ApproxError::Singular`] if the system overflows or cannot be solved.",
        "Native finite-difference calculus with physical reference scales: point,coordinate_scale,value_scale,max_evaluations,[partial index or Jacobian output count],callback. Independent D/E units; derivative E/D, Hessian/Laplacian E/D^2. References are positive. Shared callback errors and finite evaluation budgets are preserved. Curl of a three-dimensional vector field. Returns `None` for wrong dimensions.",
        "Actual native damped oscillator. Amplitude/result retain an arbitrary physical domain; angular frequency and damping have inverse-Time units, phase is dimensionless, elapsed time is Time. Damped harmonic oscillator solution. Returns position for underdamped case: x(t) = A * e^(-\u03b3t) * cos(\u03c9't + \u03c6) where \u03c9' = \u221a(\u03c9\u2080\u00b2 - \u03b3\u00b2) # Arguments * `amplitude` - Initial amplitude * `omega0` - Natural angular frequency \u03c9\u2080 * `gamma` - Damping coefficient \u03b3 * `phase` - Initial phase * `time` - Time",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Absolute value.",
        "Construct native double-double from a finite physical scalar; coherent values and physical dimensions are retained. Exact conversion from `f64`.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Builds a normalised value from an unnormalised pair.",
        "Computes the two-coordinate Euclidean norm at double-double precision. Both session-owned inputs must have the same physical dimension, which the retained result preserves. Euclidean norm of two double-double components. The inputs are scaled before squaring when needed. The result retains the low part unless the norm rounds to a subnormal or overflows.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether both parts are finite.",
        "Returns the high and low components as item0 and item1. Both have the physical dimension of the double-double input, and the low component is kept separately from the high one. Returns the stored high and low components without rounding their sum.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Square root with about 100 bits of precision. Negative inputs return NaN. Positive infinity returns infinity.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Rounds to the nearest `f64`.",
        "Native finite-difference calculus with physical reference scales: point,coordinate_scale,value_scale,max_evaluations,[partial index or Jacobian output count],callback. Independent D/E units; derivative E/D, Hessian/Laplacian E/D^2. References are positive. Shared callback errors and finite evaluation budgets are preserved. Central-difference derivative of `f` at `x`.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.",
        "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. Validates the program and returns the type and phase of every register. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`].",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. `c = a * b` for row-major `a` (`m x k`), `b` (`k x n`), `c` (`m x n`), through [`matmul_kernel`]. This is what a device without a tuned `matmul` of its own uses. # Errors [`DeviceError::Mismatch`] on wrong sizes; any error of the launch.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Reduces a whole one-column buffer on the device (see [`reduce_column`]). # Errors As [`reduce_column`].",
        "Explicit native backend specialization. Feature-disabled JIT/GPU builds return Unsupported; machine representations are normalized and source, row, fold-work and allocation budgets are checked. A backend executing on `device`.",
