        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The device kinds this *build* can offer, as [`DeviceKind::tag`]s. A compile-time fact (it does not probe hardware), so it can go in the kernel manifest. `gpu-wgpu` here means the build can drive GPUs; whether one is present is answered by `registry().list()`.",
