        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. One attempted Dormand-Prince 5(4) step per row, with per-row time and step size. Inputs: the `n_state` state columns, then `t`, then `h`. Parameters: those of `rhs`, then `t_end` and `t_done` (the time from which a row counts as finished), then `rtol` and `atol`. Outputs: the same `n_state + 2` columns after the attempt. A row whose error estimate is within tolerance advances; any other keeps its state and retries with a smaller step; a finished row is left untouched. No row waits for another. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when `rhs` is not an ODE right-hand side for `n_state` variables (see [`super::rk4_step`]).",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.",
