        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The pair `(hi, lo)` of an `f64`: `hi` is the nearest `f32`, `lo` the nearest `f32` to the remainder.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Epsilon used for tolerances on the device: `2^-23` for `F32`, `2^-52` for native `F64` and `2^-44` for double-single emulation.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Emits `ir` for the target in `options`. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when `ir` does not validate or the workgroup size is zero; [`DeviceError::Unsupported`] when the target has no type of the requested precision.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Emits the double-single WGSL module for `ir`. The bindings are those of [`super::emit`] with `array<vec2<f32>>` for `rssn_in`, `rssn_params` and `rssn_out`. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when `ir` does not validate or the workgroup size is zero.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Emits the WGSL module. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when `ir` does not validate or the workgroup size is zero.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.",
        "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. Integrates `y' = f([t,] y; params)` from `t0` to `t1 > t0` for many initial conditions at once with adaptive Dormand-Prince 5(4) steps. Every trajectory carries its own time and step size on the device ([`dopri5_step`]), so a stiff row takes small steps while the others take large ones. The host only asks, every few launches, for the minimum of the time column ([`reduce_column`]): one number crosses per check. The result for a row does not depend on the rest of the batch. # Errors Any [`DeviceError`]; [`DeviceError::Mismatch`] for `t1 < t0`, a wrong parameter count or ragged initial conditions; [`DeviceError::Backend`] when some trajectory has not arrived after `tolerance.max_launches` launches (a blow-up, or a tolerance the float type cannot meet).",
        "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. Integrates `y' = f([t,] y; params)` for many initial conditions at once with fixed-step RK4, entirely through [`Device::launch`]. `y0[i][row]` is state variable `i` of trajectory `row`. Returns the states at `t1` in the same layout. The step kernel ([`rk4_step`]) is compiled once; each of the `steps` launches advances every trajectory by `(t1 - t0) / steps`. Trajectories are independent, so the result for a row does not depend on the rest of the batch. # Errors Any [`DeviceError`]; [`DeviceError::Mismatch`] for `steps == 0`.",
        "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. Reference evaluation of row `row` of a launch of `rows` rows over `cols`: the semantics of the whole IR, fold included. `analysis` must come from [`KernelIr::analyse`] of this program; `out` receives one value per output.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The input column a gather reads, or `None` when the index is not finite, is negative, or points past the declared inputs.",
        "Explicit native backend specialization. Feature-disabled JIT/GPU builds return Unsupported; machine representations are normalized and source, row, fold-work and allocation budgets are checked. Opens `adapter`. # Errors [`DeviceError::Backend`] when the device cannot be created.",
        "Explicit native backend specialization. Feature-disabled JIT/GPU builds return Unsupported; machine representations are normalized and source, row, fold-work and allocation budgets are checked. Every usable wgpu adapter, as devices `gpu:wgpu:0`, `gpu:wgpu:1`, ... Software rasterisers (CPU adapters) are included and marked in the name.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Validates the program and returns the type and phase of every register. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`].",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Reference evaluation of one row of an elementwise launch (the semantics every device must reproduce, up to its precision): `inputs` holds that row's element of every column. Slow; for tests and fallbacks. A malformed program evaluates to NaN.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Lowers a tape. # Errors [`DeviceError::Unsupported`] when the tape contains a host call (`Call`, `Extern1`, `Extern2`); [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when it is malformed.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Whether the program is in the elementwise core: no fold and only tape instructions.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. A structural hash (constants by bit pattern): the key under which a device caches its compiled form.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Checks SSA order, index ranges, register types and phases. Every device calls this before it runs or emits a program, so a malformed program cannot index outside a register file or a buffer. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`].",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. A short stable tag: `cpu`, `cpu-parallel`, `gpu-wgpu`, `gpu-cuda`...",
