        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Upload, launch, download: `columns[i][row]` in, one vector per output out. The simple path; hold [`Buffer`]s yourself to keep data on the device between launches. # Errors Any [`DeviceError`].",
        "Execute the actual native device kernel with heterogeneous measured input columns, parameters and output units from a retained tape reference frame.",
        "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. `op` over every output of `map` applied to `columns`, fused: one value per output of `map`, and no mapped column is ever stored. # Errors Any [`DeviceError`]; [`DeviceError::Mismatch`] when the columns differ in length or number.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The first pass of a fused map-reduce. `map` (elementwise, any number of inputs and outputs) is evaluated inside the reduction block and each of its outputs is combined with `op`. The mapped columns never exist. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when `map` is not elementwise or uses `gather`.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. `C = A * B` for row-major `A` (`m x k`, column 0) and `B` (`k x n`, column 1), one row of the launch per element of `C` (`m * n` rows). Parameter 0 is `n`; `k` follows from the length of `B`. # Errors Never in practice; the kernel is fixed.",
        "Explicit native backend specialization. Feature-disabled JIT/GPU builds return Unsupported; machine representations are normalized and source, row, fold-work and allocation budgets are checked. Lowers and compiles `ir`; `None` when either step fails.",
