        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The type of the value this instruction defines (`select` takes the type of its branches, which [`KernelIr::analyse`] resolves; here it reports a number).",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The defaults for `target`: `f32`, workgroups of 64, entry `main` (`rssn_main` where `main` is reserved).",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The same options with another precision.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Packs columns into one column-major host vector. # Errors [`DeviceError::Mismatch`] when the columns differ in length.",
        "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. An all-pairs interaction over `columns` attribute columns. `pair` is elementwise with `2 * columns` inputs, the attributes of body `i` followed by those of body `j`, and any number of outputs; output `k` of the result is the `op`-combination over every `j` of output `k` of `pair`. With `skip_self` the term `j == i` is left out. The attributes of body `i` are loaded once per row, not once per pair. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when `pair` does not have that shape.",
        "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. Adds a kernel reading `inputs` (one source per input column of `ir`) with the uniform `params`. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when the kernel does not validate, the counts do not match, or a source names a later kernel, a missing output or a missing external column.",
        "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. Merges every producer into a consumer that reads it, as far as the rules in the module documentation allow. Returns the number of launches removed.",
        "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. The number of launches [`Plan::run`] performs.",
        "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. A plan over `externals` input columns.",
        "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. Asks for `source` to be returned by [`Plan::run`] (results come back in the order they were asked for). # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] for a source that does not exist.",
        "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. Runs the plan on `device`: `externals[i]` is external column `i` (`rows` values each). Returns the requested results. # Errors [`DeviceError::Mismatch`] when a column has the wrong length or the count of externals is wrong; any error of the device.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. `F64` when the device has it, else `F32`.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.",
        "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. Reduces column `column` of `buffer`, whose columns have the lengths `lens`, to one number, on the device. Only the final value crosses to the host. An empty column gives the identity of `op`. # Errors Any [`DeviceError`]; [`DeviceError::Unsupported`] on a device without structured kernels.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. `acc \u2218 x`.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The neutral element.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. One pass of a tree reduction over column `column` of a buffer with `inputs` columns: row `r` combines elements `r * FAN_IN ..` of that column. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when `column >= inputs`.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The device to use when the caller names none: the first GPU, else the parallel CPU with at least two workers, else the sequential CPU or any registered device.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. A registry with no devices.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The first device of a kind.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The device with this id.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The process-wide registry (created on first use).",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Descriptions of every device, in registration order.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. A registry holding the built-in CPU devices (and, with feature `gpu-wgpu`, every adapter wgpu finds; none is not an error).",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Adds a device. # Errors [`DeviceError::Mismatch`] when the id is taken.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Checks that `rhs` is an ODE right-hand side for `n_state` variables and reports whether it takes the time as input 0. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`].",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. One classical Runge-Kutta 4 step of `y' = f([t,] y)` as a kernel. `rhs` has `n_state` outputs and either `n_state` inputs (autonomous) or `n_state + 1` with the time as input 0. The step kernel has `n_state` inputs (the state columns of every trajectory), the parameters of `rhs` followed by two more, `t` at index `rhs.params` and the step `h` at `rhs.params + 1`, and `n_state` outputs (the next state). Launching it `steps` times with a changing `t` integrates every row, that is every initial condition, with the same program: the ODE-ensemble pattern. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when the shape of `rhs` does not match, or when `rhs` is not elementwise or uses `gather` (which addresses columns and cannot be composed).",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. One classical Runge-Kutta 4 step of `y' = f([t,] y)` as a kernel. `rhs` has `n_state` outputs and either `n_state` inputs (autonomous) or `n_state + 1` with the time as input 0. The step kernel has `n_state` inputs (the state columns of every trajectory), the parameters of `rhs` followed by two more, `t` at index `rhs.params` and the step `h` at `rhs.params + 1`, and `n_state` outputs (the next state). Launching it `steps` times with a changing `t` integrates every row, that is every initial condition, with the same program: the ODE-ensemble pattern. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when the shape of `rhs` does not match, or when `rhs` is not elementwise or uses `gather` (which addresses columns and cannot be composed).",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Launches `ir` over host columns of independent lengths and downloads the outputs, one vector per output column. # Errors Any [`DeviceError`].",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. `select` takes its first branch unless the condition is exactly zero.",
        "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. `y = A x` for a CSR matrix: column 0 the row pointers (`rows + 1` entries), column 1 the column indices, column 2 the values, column 3 the vector. One row of the launch per matrix row. Row pointers and column indices are stored as floats, so they are exact below `2^24` on an `f32` device (`2^53` on an `f64` one). # Errors Never in practice; the kernel is fixed.",
        "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. A 1-D stencil: `out[r] = sum of weight * x[r + offset]` over `points`. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when `points` is empty or an offset does not fit 32 bits.",
        "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. A 2-D stencil on a row-major `ny x nx` grid stored in one column. `out[y][x] = sum of weight * u[y + dy][x + dx]` over `points` (`(dx, dy, weight)`). Parameter 0 is `nx`; `ny` follows from the column length. The boundary rule applies per axis. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when `points` is empty or an offset does not fit 32 bits.",
        "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch.",
