        "Construct a native distribution enum in normalized sample coordinates, then restore an explicit positive sample reference scale. All15 named variants are supported. Continuous density has inverse sample units; discrete probability mass remains dimensionless.",
        "Native normalized density restored by the explicit reference scale. For discrete variants this is probability mass and has no physical units. The probability density (or mass) at `x`.",
        "Native inverse CDF restored to sample units. Valid infinite endpoint quantiles are preserved. The `u`-quantile, `0 \u2264 u \u2264 1`: the inverse of [`Distribution::cdf`]. Closed-form inverses are used when available. Other continuous distributions invert the CDF by bracketed bisection, and discrete distributions search for the smallest supported count whose CDF reaches `u`. # Errors [`DistError::Domain`] when `u` is outside `[0, 1]` or a parameter is unusable.",
        "Native FnMut uniform-source specialization using the shared session-owned Rng. Both distribution and random stream kinds are checked; result retains sample units. One sample, from a uniform source on `[0, 1)`. # Errors [`DistError::Domain`] for a parameter the sampler cannot use.",
