        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Returns the point as a vector from the origin.",
        "Intersect a prepared triangle and a ray with matching coordinate dimensions. Inclusive bounds use the same dimension as the coordinates. The minimum is finite and nonnegative. A Some upper bound is finite and None is unbounded. The hit record contains physical t and point plus a dimensionless unit normal. Intersects a ray over the inclusive parameter interval `[min_t, max_t]`. The lower bound is finite and nonnegative. The upper bound may be positive infinity. The returned normal follows the vertex winding. Zero directions and rays numerically parallel to the plane have no hit. Near a triangle edge or range endpoint, the signs are checked over the exact binary-float inputs.",
        "Intersect at most 4096 origin handles with a common dimensionless unit direction. Origins and inclusive bounds share the triangle coordinate dimension. The minimum is finite and nonnegative. A Some upper bound is finite and None is unbounded. The record has hit_mask and physical t of shape [n], physical points and dimensionless normals of shape [n,3]. Misses have zero placeholders and no result handles are retained. Intersects parallel rays with a common direction and parameter range. Results follow the order of `origins`, using the same bounds as [`Self::intersect`]. Rays along the projection axis are culled against the triangle's projected bounding box. An invalid shared setting gives no hits.",
        "Prepare three point handles with one coordinate dimension and a positive finite reference in that dimension. Degenerate triangles return None. The resulting handle owns its geometry. Prepares the triangle or returns `None` for invalid or collinear vertices.",
