        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The subgroup `{g \u2208 G : property(g)}`, which must be a subgroup. `prune(level, point, image)` may reject a partial element as soon as it maps the base point `point` to `image`: return `false` when no element of the subgroup can do that. Pruning must never reject a subgroup element; it only makes the search faster.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. A Sylow `p`-subgroup. Grows a `p`-subgroup `P` by `p`-elements of its normaliser outside it until `|P|` is the full power of `p` dividing `|G|` (a `p`-subgroup is Sylow exactly when `p` does not divide `[N(P) : P]`, so a `p`-element of `N(P) \\\\ P` exists until then). `None` if random sampling failed `max_tries` times in a row.",
