        "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased. The second derivative on `f64`. These are the classical formulas. `abs`, `floor` and `ceil` report zero everywhere, including at their kinks, where the derivative does not exist.",
        "Transform a finite rank-one half spectrum with n/2 + 1 bins, or zero bins for n = 0. Imaginary DC and even Nyquist components do not contribute. Returns n real 1/n-normalized samples as a measured tensor with the spectrum's physical units. In Rust, IrfftPlan::apply_into writes into a caller-owned output slice. Writes one inverse real FFT to the supplied sample slice. # Errors Returns [`IrfftError::Shape`] and leaves the output untouched unless both slices match the plan.",
        "Prepare a fixed-length inverse real FFT for repeated half spectra in this session. Supply the number of real output samples, from 0 through 262143. This determines odd or even transform parity and the required bin count. The plan holds the even-length unpacking factors. Prepares an inverse transform whose output has `n` real samples. # Errors Returns [`IrfftError::Length`] if the output or FFT workspace size exceeds the maximum size of a slice.",
        "Report the number of real samples produced by this session's inverse real FFT plan. Real sample count of the inverse transform.",
        "Report the number of half-spectrum bins required by this session's inverse real FFT plan. The empty plan requires zero bins. Number of nonredundant bins, or zero for an empty transform.",
        "Measure a seeded periodic two-dimensional Ising lattice after thermalization, then sample after each positive stride within the requested sweeps. A physical frame accepts temperature in kelvin and converts it using Boltzmann's constant. Return final row-major spins, sample count and per-site observables. Energy uses the frame's energy units, susceptibility uses inverse energy and heat capacity is reported over Boltzmann's constant. Binder is None when all measured magnetizations are zero. Sweeps and measurements count toward the site-work budget. Measures a seeded periodic 2D checkerboard Ising run after thermalization. Discards `thermalisation` sweeps, then runs `params.mc_steps` more. Measures after every `sample_every` sweeps in the latter interval and returns the final spins alongside the per-site averages. Incomplete sampling intervals still advance the spins. Measurements use constant extra storage and do not consume random draws. The bond energy counts the right and lower bond of every spin. Unit axes therefore contribute a constant self-bond energy, and extent-two axes have two bonds between the same pair. Susceptibility uses the variance of absolute magnetization. Binder is NaN when all measured magnetizations vanish. # Errors Returns an error for an invalid lattice, an overflowing sweep total, no complete measurement interval, or a nonpositive temperature or nonfinite inverse temperature.",
        "IO: execute the original native hard-coded phase-transition scenario, create its caller-selected output directory and write CSV/NPY files. Explicit work acknowledgement requires205million site updates. Coordinates/temperature are the original reduced-unit demonstration; no physical values are silently erased. An example scenario that simulates the Ising model across a range of temperatures to observe the phase transition. # Errors This function will return an error if it fails to reshape the `Array2<f64>` for NPY output or if it fails to create or write to the output files (CSV or NPY). The files `ising_low_temp_state.npy`, `ising_high_temp_state.npy` and `ising_magnetization_vs_temp.csv` are written into `output_dir`, which is created if missing.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Runs an Ising model simulation with the fixed seed [`DEFAULT_ISING_SEED`]. Equivalent to [`run_ising_simulation_seeded`]; repeated calls with the same parameters return identical results.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Runs an Ising model simulation whose random numbers all derive from `seed`. The initial configuration and every row update use their own generator derived from `seed`, so the result does not depend on thread scheduling. Grids with an axis of length one or two use ordered single-site sweeps. At positive temperature on a multi-site grid, each visit in such a sweep proposes a flip with probability one half.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Monte Carlo of a spin model on a hypercubic lattice of any dimension. Ising, Potts, XY or Heisenberg on a lattice of **any** dimension `D` (periodic or open), delegating to [`crate::sim::spin_models`]. Returns the per-site averages over `sweeps` measurements after `thermalisation` updates. # Errors Fails for invalid lattices, `temperature <= 0` or unsupported model/algorithm combinations (for example cluster updates with a field).",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Monte Carlo of a spin model on a hypercubic lattice of any dimension. Ising, Potts, XY or Heisenberg on a lattice of **any** dimension `D` (periodic or open), delegating to [`crate::sim::spin_models`]. Returns the per-site averages over `sweeps` measurements after `thermalisation` updates. # Errors Fails for invalid lattices, `temperature <= 0` or unsupported model/algorithm combinations (for example cluster updates with a field).",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Monte Carlo of a spin model on a hypercubic lattice of any dimension. Ising, Potts, XY or Heisenberg on a lattice of **any** dimension `D` (periodic or open), delegating to [`crate::sim::spin_models`]. Returns the per-site averages over `sweeps` measurements after `thermalisation` updates. # Errors Fails for invalid lattices, `temperature <= 0` or unsupported model/algorithm combinations (for example cluster updates with a field).",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The Wolff single-cluster algorithm: a cluster grown from a random seed spin, each aligned neighbour added with probability `1 - exp(-2/T)`, is flipped as a whole. Rejection-free and free of critical slowing down, so it samples near `T_c` far better than local Metropolis updates. `sweeps` cluster updates are measured after `thermalisation` discarded ones. Runs on the dimension-generic engine [`crate::sim::spin_models::OnModel`] (cold start, periodic `width x height` lattice); the observables are `NaN` for lattices the engine rejects (periodic sides below 3).",
        "Native finite-difference calculus with physical reference scales: point,coordinate_scale,value_scale,max_evaluations,[partial index or Jacobian output count],callback. Independent D/E units; derivative E/D, Hessian/Laplacian E/D^2. References are positive. Shared callback errors and finite evaluation budgets are preserved. Jacobian of `f: R^n -> R^m` at `point`, in row-major order (`m` rows of `n` entries). `f` writes its `m` outputs into its second argument.",
        "Actual feature-gated native JIT adapter. Requires RSSN jit; disabled builds return Unsupported. Compiled expression calls retain physical tape frames; low-level LIR has explicit normalized values and bounded acyclic control flow. A cache fingerprint of `tape` under this backend's context. Internal lookup also checks full program equality, so collisions of this fingerprint cannot alias native code.",
        "Actual feature-gated native JIT adapter. Requires RSSN jit; disabled builds return Unsupported. Compiled expression calls retain physical tape frames; low-level LIR has explicit normalized values and bounded acyclic control flow. Number of distinct programs compiled so far.",
        "Actual feature-gated native JIT adapter. Requires RSSN jit; disabled builds return Unsupported. Compiled expression calls retain physical tape frames; low-level LIR has explicit normalized values and bounded acyclic control flow. Compile an already-lowered tape through the exact program cache. Concurrent callers for the same tape share one compilation and code owner. Optimize the tape first when desired; this method preserves the supplied instruction order and validates it before native code emission. # Errors Returns [`BackendError::Codegen`] for an invalid tape, unsupported host, or a code-generation failure.",
        "Actual feature-gated native JIT adapter. Requires RSSN jit; disabled builds return Unsupported. Compiled expression calls retain physical tape frames; low-level LIR has explicit normalized values and bounded acyclic control flow. The context key mixed into every cache key.",
