        "Native finite-difference calculus with physical reference scales: point,coordinate_scale,value_scale,max_evaluations,[partial index or Jacobian output count],callback. Independent D/E units; derivative E/D, Hessian/Laplacian E/D^2. References are positive. Shared callback errors and finite evaluation budgets are preserved. Laplacian of a scalar field, using only the diagonal Hessian stencil.",
        "Physical native series/sequence convergence. sum_series: start,max_terms,tolerance,value_scale,max_evaluations,term(Float)->E. sequence_limit omits start. Levin: max_terms,value_scale,max_evaluations,term(Int)->E; result includes native error estimate. References/tolerances are positive physical E; callback failures propagate and budgets bound actual host calls. Sums `term(0) + term(1) + ...` with a Levin transformation of the first `n_terms` partial sums. Returns `(estimate, error_estimate)` where the error estimate is the difference of the two highest-order transforms; the best (smallest successive difference) transform is reported. Prefer [`levin_sum_lazy`] when the terms are available directly, since this path differences the partial sums to recover them. # Errors Returns an error if fewer than four terms are requested or no finite transform could be formed.",
        "Physical native series/sequence convergence. sum_series: start,max_terms,tolerance,value_scale,max_evaluations,term(Float)->E. sequence_limit omits start. Levin: max_terms,value_scale,max_evaluations,term(Int)->E; result includes native error estimate. References/tolerances are positive physical E; callback failures propagate and budgets bound actual host calls. Sums `term(0) + term(1) + ...` with a Levin transformation of the first `n_terms` partial sums. Returns `(estimate, error_estimate)` where the error estimate is the difference of the two highest-order transforms; the best (smallest successive difference) transform is reported. Prefer [`levin_sum_lazy`] when the terms are available directly, since this path differences the partial sums to recover them. # Errors Returns an error if fewer than four terms are requested or no finite transform could be formed.",
        "Physical native series/sequence convergence. sum_series: start,max_terms,tolerance,value_scale,max_evaluations,term(Float)->E. sequence_limit omits start. Levin: max_terms,value_scale,max_evaluations,term(Int)->E; result includes native error estimate. References/tolerances are positive physical E; callback failures propagate and budgets bound actual host calls. Sums `term(0) + term(1) + ...` with a Levin transformation of the first `n_terms` partial sums. Returns `(estimate, error_estimate)` where the error estimate is the difference of the two highest-order transforms; the best (smallest successive difference) transform is reported. Prefer [`levin_sum_lazy`] when the terms are available directly, since this path differences the partial sums to recover them. # Errors Returns an error if fewer than four terms are requested or no finite transform could be formed.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The matrix of `ad x`: column `j` holds the coordinates of `[x, e_j]`.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. `[x, y]` in coordinates.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The span of all `[a_i, b_j]` (echelon basis).",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The Cartan matrix of type `letter` and rank `n`.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Cartan's first criterion: `g` is solvable iff `K(g, [g, g]) = 0`.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. A Cartan subalgebra: the generalised zero eigenspace of a regular element, chosen among dense and sparse pseudo-random candidates for the smallest dimension and then for the most rational roots (sparse candidates find the split tori of matrix algebras with a diagonal part).",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The quadratic Casimir operator `sum K^{ab} rho(e_a) rho(e_b)` of a representation `rho` (one matrix per basis element) for the Killing form; the algebra must be semisimple.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The center.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The characteristic polynomial `det(x I - m)` as coefficients of `x^0 ..= x^n` (Faddeev-LeVerrier).",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The connected components (as index lists) of the Dynkin diagram.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The derived series `g \u2287 [g, g] \u2287 ...` up to the point it stabilises.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The standard simple roots of a type in Euclidean coordinates. Those of Bourbaki, not normalised to a common length: `A_n` lives in `R^{n+1}`, the exceptional `E`-types in `R^8`, `F_4` in `R^4`, `G_2` in `R^3`.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. A Lie algebra from structure constants; `None` unless the bracket is antisymmetric and satisfies the Jacobi identity.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The Lie algebra spanned by a basis of rational matrices. Returns `None` unless the basis is nonempty, consists of square matrices of the same positive order, and is independent and closed under the commutator. The structure constants use the input basis order.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether the lower central series reaches zero.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Cartan's second criterion: `g` is semisimple iff `K` is nondegenerate.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether the derived series reaches zero.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether the span of `vectors` is closed under the bracket.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The Killing form `K_ab = tr(ad e_a ad e_b)`.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. A Levi decomposition `g = s \u22c9 r`: a semisimple subalgebra `s` complementary to the radical `r` (returned as `(s, r)`), lifted through the derived series of `r` (Whitehead's lemma makes each lift a linear problem).",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The lower central series `g \u2287 [g, g] \u2287 [g, [g, g]] \u2287 ...`.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Parses a type name such as `A2`, `E8`, `G2`.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The positive roots of the root system with Cartan matrix `a`, in simple-root coordinates, ordered by height (the root strings through the simple roots are followed level by level).",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The radical (largest solvable ideal) `= [g, g]^\u22a5` for the Killing form.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The distinct rational roots of the polynomial with coefficients `p[0] ..= p[n]` (rational root theorem); `None` if the coefficients are too large to factor.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The simple factors of the algebra with Cartan matrix `a` as `(letter, rank)` pairs, or `None` if `a` is not the Cartan matrix of a semisimple Lie algebra.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The decomposition of `g` into simultaneous generalised eigenspaces of `ad h` for the abelian subalgebra spanned by `h`. Only roots with rational values are found; the second component counts the dimensions that belong to other (irrational or complex) roots.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The standard basis of a classical matrix Lie algebra. Matrices of Gaussian integers (`gl`, `sl`: elementary matrices and the Chevalley `H_k = E_kk - E_{k+1,k+1}`; `so(n)`: `E_ij - E_ji`; `sp(2n)`: `[[A, B], [C, -A^T]]` with `B`, `C` symmetric; `su(n)`: `E_ij - E_ji`, `i (E_ij + E_ji)`, `i H_k`).",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The upper central series `0 \u2286 Z_1 \u2286 Z_2 \u2286 ...` (without the leading 0).",
        "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Emits `inst` assigning an existing register.",
        "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Ends the current block with a bail.",
        "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Lowers a tape to a *batch* function that evaluates it at every row. The function's parameters are the input columns (`inputs` slices), the parameter vector (one slice), the output columns (`outputs` slices) and the row count (`I64`): for `row < rows` it stores output `k` of `row` into `out_k[row]`. Missing input elements read NaN, exactly like [`Compiled::call_batch`](super::Compiled::call_batch). Constants and parameters are loop-invariant and evaluated once before the loop. Every row gets the bits [`Tape::eval`](super::tape::Tape::eval) gives it: each tape instruction maps to the LIR instruction with the same IEEE semantics. Returns `None` for tapes with `Gather` (its column is chosen per row, which a column-per-parameter signature cannot express).",
        "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Adds a parameter of type `ty` to `block`.",
        "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Ends the current block with a conditional branch.",
        "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. A function with the given parameter and result types; the builder is positioned in the entry block.",
        "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Checks host arguments against a function's parameters. # Errors Unknown function, wrong arity or types, or a read-only slice for a function that writes, or a function returning a slice.",
        "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. The block being emitted into.",
        "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. `x` truncated toward zero to an integer, or `None` for NaN and values outside the `i64` range (the bail condition of [`Inst::FToI`]).",
        "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. The comparison of two floats.",
        "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. The finished function. # Errors A block without a terminator.",
        "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. The float maximum with NaN propagation.",
