        "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Checks types, arities and references. # Errors The first problem found.",
        "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. The comparison of two integers.",
        "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Emits `inst` into a fresh register of its natural type and returns it. For [`Inst::Call`] and [`Inst::Copy`], whose type is not determined by the instruction alone, use [`FunctionBuilder::ins_typed`].",
        "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Emits `inst` into a fresh register of type `ty`.",
        "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps.",
        "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Runs `func` in the reference interpreter with at most `max_steps` instructions (a runaway loop bails with [`BAIL_STEPS`]). # Errors The module does not verify, or the arguments do not match the function's parameters, or a read-only slice is passed to a function that writes.",
        "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Whether the current block already has its terminator.",
        "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Ends the current block with a jump.",
