        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Incorporate one observation. # Errors Reports a dimension mismatch, non-finite input, or arithmetic overflow.",
        "Atomically incorporate a row-major tensor of observations with the accumulator's coordinate units. Columns must match the accumulator dimension. Incorporate a flat row-major batch atomically. Each row contains [`Self::dimension`] values. Large batches use bounded shards and combine them in row order, independent of worker count. An empty batch leaves the accumulator unchanged. # Errors Returns an error for an incomplete row, non-finite input, count or arithmetic overflow, or failure to allocate a shard.",
        "Atomically incorporate a row-major tensor of observations with the accumulator's coordinate units and one nonnegative, dimensionless integer frequency per row. Each frequency counts repeated observations without expanding the tensor. Incorporate a flat row-major batch with an integer frequency per row. Each row represents as many identical observations as its frequency, with no need to expand those observations. A zero frequency adds no observations. All row values must be finite. The resulting count is the sum of frequencies and the previous count. Sample covariance divides by the resulting count minus one. Floating-point results can differ from pushing each repetition individually. Shards and their merge order are independent of worker count. # Errors An incomplete row, a frequency vector of the wrong length, a non-finite value, count or arithmetic overflow, or a shard allocation failure leaves the accumulator unchanged.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Unbiased sample covariance (divisor `n - 1`), or `None` for fewer than two observations.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Approximate minimum degree ordering of the pattern `adj`. Returns `perm` with `perm[new] = old` (a permutation of `0..adj.len()`). The pattern must be symmetric. Duplicate entries and self loops do not affect the ordering. # Panics A neighbour index is outside `0..adj.len()`.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Number of nonzeros of the Cholesky factor `L` (including the diagonal) of the pattern `adj` ordered by `perm` (`perm[new] = old`), by symbolic factorisation along the elimination tree.",
        "Measures the permuted half-bandwidth and lower-triangle profile from CSR adjacency offsets and neighbour indices. The zero-based permutation maps each new position to its old vertex. Single-direction and repeated edges describe the same undirected pattern. Measures the bandwidth and profile of a permuted sparse pattern. `perm[new] = old` names the original vertex at each reordered position. Edges may be listed in either or both directions. Duplicate and diagonal entries leave both metrics unchanged. The work is linear in the number of vertices and listed edges, with linear storage in the vertex count. # Errors The permutation is malformed, a neighbour is out of range, or the accumulated profile does not fit a `usize`.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Best of approximate minimum degree and multilevel nested dissection. Two leaf sizes are tried and judged by the exact symbolic Cholesky fill ([`cholesky_fill`]); the result is never worse than [`amd_order`] and, on large two- and three-dimensional meshes, usually better.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Multilevel nested dissection ordering of the pattern `adj` (see the module documentation). Returns `perm` with `perm[new] = old`.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. As [`multilevel_nested_dissection_order`] with explicit parameters.",
