        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Nested dissection ordering by recursive level-structure bisection. Pieces of at most 300 vertices are ordered by [`amd_order`]; larger connected pieces are split by a vertex separator taken from a BFS level structure rooted at a pseudo-peripheral vertex (the level near the middle with the best size/balance trade-off, pruned of vertices without neighbours on the far side); separators are numbered after both halves.",
        "Compute the full linear convolution of a real recording with the prepared filter. The output has sample units times tap units. Empty recordings give an empty measured tensor. The result has at most 262144 values. Applies the filter with zero extension and returns the full convolution. # Errors Errors on non-finite inputs or output, or an unallocatable output extent.",
        "Convolve up to 4096 real recordings sharing one sample dimension. Supply flat samples and zero-based row offsets; repeated offsets represent empty recordings. Returns output offsets and flat values with sample units times tap units. The whole batch has at most 262144 output values. Applies this prepared filter to several recordings in input order. Each result has the same length and zero extension as [`Self::apply`]. Empty recordings give empty results. Independent recordings can run in parallel under the active execution policy. # Errors Returns the error for the first recording that fails [`Self::apply`].",
        "Prepare the spectrum of a measured real filter with at most 65536 taps. The immutable handle retains the tap units and can be reused for several recordings in this session. Creates a plan for a real finite impulse response filter. # Errors Errors for an empty or non-finite filter, a non-finite transform or an unallocatable FFT extent.",
        "Native disjoint mutable chunk scheduling specializes mutation to returning a replacement vector of identical chunk length and units, including the short final chunk. Checked owner-thread callbacks preserve failure and budget semantics. Runs `f(i, row)` over mutable chunks of `data` of `chunk` elements each (`i` is the chunk index); sequential when there are fewer than `grain` chunks. The chunks are disjoint, so the result cannot depend on the scheduling.",
        "Native mutable parallel map specializes mutation to returning a replacement value. The input tensor is owned/copied; outputs retain identical physical units and original index semantics. Runs `f(i, &mut items[i])` for every element, in parallel when there are at least `grain` elements. Each element is touched by exactly one call, so the outcome is independent of the scheduling.",
        "Actual native parallel map with host callbacks serviced serially on their owning thread. Index order and native Rayon scheduling are retained; every worker is joined and callback failures/budgets are propagated. Maps `0..n` through `f` and collects in index order. Runs sequentially when `n < grain` (or `n < 2`).",
