        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. One Swendsen-Wang sweep with a random embedding direction; returns the number of clusters. A non-zero field is included through the ghost spin `sign(h) e_0`: the cluster attached to the ghost is never flipped. A ferromagnetic `j2 > 0` joins the bond set and the clusters stay independent. An antiferromagnetic `j2 < 0` is frustrated, so it stays out of the bond set; its Boltzmann factor then couples the orientations of *pairs* of clusters and they are no longer independent, so the sweep becomes a cluster-level Metropolis: every cluster is flipped atomically, in a fixed order, and accepted with `min(1, exp(-beta dE))`, `dE` being the change of `2 J2 sum p_i p_j` over the diagonal bonds that cross it, evaluated against the configuration left by the clusters already flipped in the same sweep (`p_i = s_i . r` is the projection on the embedding direction, see [`Self::wolff_step`]). Both branches are exact; for `j2 < 0` only the independence of the clusters \u2014 and hence the reading of the sweep as independent Fortuin-Kasteleyn clusters \u2014 is lost. # Errors Fails for `J <= 0`.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. One Swendsen-Wang sweep with a random embedding direction; returns the number of clusters. A non-zero field is included through the ghost spin `sign(h) e_0`: the cluster attached to the ghost is never flipped. A ferromagnetic `j2 > 0` joins the bond set and the clusters stay independent. An antiferromagnetic `j2 < 0` is frustrated, so it stays out of the bond set; its Boltzmann factor then couples the orientations of *pairs* of clusters and they are no longer independent, so the sweep becomes a cluster-level Metropolis: every cluster is flipped atomically, in a fixed order, and accepted with `min(1, exp(-beta dE))`, `dE` being the change of `2 J2 sum p_i p_j` over the diagonal bonds that cross it, evaluated against the configuration left by the clusters already flipped in the same sweep (`p_i = s_i . r` is the projection on the embedding direction, see [`Self::wolff_step`]). Both branches are exact; for `j2 < 0` only the independence of the clusters \u2014 and hence the reading of the sweep as independent Fortuin-Kasteleyn clusters \u2014 is lost. # Errors Fails for `J <= 0`.",
