        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Replica-exchange Wang-Landau with several walkers per energy window. After Vogel, Li, Wuest and Landau (2013): the energy range is split into overlapping windows, each window runs its own Wang-Landau iteration with `walkers` walkers sharing `ln g`, neighbouring windows exchange configurations with probability `min(1, g_i(E_a) g_j(E_b) / (g_i(E_b) g_j(E_a)))`, and the per-window densities of states are joined at the overlap bin where their logarithmic derivatives agree best. Works for the Ising model (`N = 1`) and continuous O(N) spins. Returns `(bin centre, ln g)` for the visited bins, normalised to `sum g = 1`. # Errors Fails for invalid options, lattice errors, or if a walker cannot be placed in its window.",
        "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Replica-exchange Wang-Landau with several walkers per energy window. After Vogel, Li, Wuest and Landau (2013): the energy range is split into overlapping windows, each window runs its own Wang-Landau iteration with `walkers` walkers sharing `ln g`, neighbouring windows exchange configurations with probability `min(1, g_i(E_a) g_j(E_b) / (g_i(E_b) g_j(E_a)))`, and the per-window densities of states are joined at the overlap bin where their logarithmic derivatives agree best. Works for the Ising model (`N = 1`) and continuous O(N) spins. Returns `(bin centre, ln g)` for the visited bins, normalised to `sum g = 1`. # Errors Fails for invalid options, lattice errors, or if a walker cannot be placed in its window.",
