        "`permutations(n, k)`: number of `k`-permutations of `n` items, `n! / (n - k)!`. Computes the number of permutations `P(n, k) = n! / (n-k)!`. # Arguments * `n` - The total number of items. * `k` - The number of items to choose. # Returns The number of permutations as an `f64`. Returns `0.0` if `k > n`.",
        "Computes persistence intervals `list(birth, death)` per dimension up to `max_dim` by tracking Betti numbers over `steps + 1` radii up to `max_eps`.",
        "Computes persistent homology barcodes over `Z/2` for a filtered complex up to `max_dim`, returning `list(birth, death)` pairs per dimension. Exact persistent homology over `Z/2` of a filtered simplicial complex. `filtration` lists `(value, simplex)` pairs in any order; every proper face of a simplex must be present with a value no larger than the simplex's. A repeated simplex enters at its earliest value, and both signs of zero share a filtration level. Simplices are ordered by value, then dimension, then lexicographically. The boundary matrix is reduced by the standard left-to-right column algorithm with *clearing* (the twist optimisation): dimensions are processed from the top down, and a column that is the pivot of a reduced column of the next dimension is known to reduce to zero and is skipped. Returns one [`PersistenceDiagram`] per dimension `0..=max_dim`; each interval is an exact `(birth, death)` pair of filtration values and a class that never dies has `death = f64::INFINITY`. Zero-length intervals are omitted. Intervals are sorted by birth then death. # Errors [`PersistenceError::InvalidFiltration`] if the input is not a filtration.",
