        "`polygon(vertices)`: closed polygonal contour through `list(z1, ..., zn)` in order.",
        "`polylog(s, z)`: polylogarithm `Li_s(z) = sum_{k=1}^infty z^k / k^s`. The polylogarithm `Li_s(z)` for real `s` and real `z`. Real on `z <= 1` (including the negative axis); for `z > 1` the principal value is complex in general and `NaN` is returned, except for non-positive integer `s`, where `Li_{-n}(z)` is the real rational function `z A_n(z)/(1-z)^(n+1)`. At `z = 1` the analytic continuation `\u03b6(s)` is returned (and `+\u221e` at the pole `s = 1`).",
        "`polylog_complex(s, re, im)`: `list(re, im)` of `Li_s(z)`. The polylogarithm `Li_s(z)` for complex `s` and `z`, on the principal branch (cut along `[1, \u221e)`). * `|z| <= 1/2`: the defining power series; * non-positive integer `s = -n`: the rational function `z A_n(z)/(1-z)^(n+1)` with Eulerian numbers `A_n`; * positive integer `s`: the logarithmic (Bernoulli/Hurwitz) continuation for `|z| <= 3/2` and Kummer's inversion relation beyond, so every `z` is covered; * real `s >= -15.5` and real `z < 1` outside the series' fast region: the same continuation as [`lerch`] with `a = 1`; * other `s`: the logarithmic expansion about `z = 1` for `|ln z| < 4.5` (the expansion is valid for `|ln z| < 2\u03c0`, but `\u03b6(s-k)` overflows `f64` before it converges near that bound); * `z = 1`: `\u03b6(s)` (the analytic continuation, as in `mpmath`). Outside the stated domain the result is `NaN + NaN i`. Accuracy is about `1e-13` for moderate parameters.",
        "`polynomial_regression(xs, ys, degree)`: polynomial least-squares fit returning coefficients `list(c0, c1, ..., cd)` up to degree `degree`.",
        "`polynomial_system_roots(system)`: finite roots of a square polynomial system by total-degree homotopy continuation as `list(list(re, im), ...)`. Solves a square polynomial system by total-degree homotopy continuation. Solves the square polynomial system `system[i] = 0` (terms of equation `i`, exponent vectors with one entry per variable) by total-degree homotopy continuation in projective coordinates with a Cauchy endgame and path-jumping protection; see the module documentation. One [`PathEnd`] is returned per start solution (the product of the degrees). Regular finite endpoints are Newton-polished; singular finite endpoints and endpoints at infinity are classified with their winding number. [`HomotopyOptions::precision`] selects double, double-double or adaptive extended-precision tracking. # Errors [`RootError::Invalid`] for an empty system, exponent vectors of the wrong length, nonfinite coefficients, equations without a positive declared degree, or a product of equation degrees above 100 000.",
        "`pooled_t_test(xs, ys)`: two-sample pooled t-test returning `list(statistic, p_value)` assuming equal population variances.",
