        "`qed_lagrangian(psibar, psi, A, m, e)`: symbolic QED Lagrangian density for Dirac spinor `psi` and gauge field `A`.",
        "`qm_apply(A, psi)`: applies quantum operator `A` to wavefunction `psi`.",
        "`qp_eq(Q, c, A, b)`: solves the equality-constrained quadratic program `min 1/2 x^T Q x + c^T x` subject to `A x = b`.",
        "`qp_solve(q, c, a, rel, b, bounds)`: `list(x, objective, iterations, active)` minimising `0.5 x'Qx + c'x` subject to `a x (rel) b` and `bounds` (`list(list(lo, hi), ..)`, `inf` for no upper bound). Solves a convex quadratic program. # Errors Returns an error string when the dimensions disagree, when an entry is not finite, when `q` has a negative eigenvalue (a non-convex problem), when the problem is infeasible, when a positive semidefinite problem is unbounded below on its feasible set, or when the active-set iteration exceeds `max_iter`.",
        "`qr(A)`: QR factorization `list(Q, R)` with orthogonal `Q` and upper triangular `R`.",
        "`qr_pivoted_diagonal(a)`: non-increasing absolute diagonal `|R_ii|` from column-pivoted QR of `a`. Column-pivoted Householder QR (Businger and Golub). At each step the remaining column of largest norm is brought forward, so the diagonal of `R` decreases in magnitude and its decay reveals the numerical rank. Column norms are downdated and recomputed when cancellation makes the downdate unreliable. Each reflector applies to contiguous columns, with large independent column batches running in parallel. # Errors [`LowRankError::Shape`] for inconsistent storage or non-finite entries, and [`LowRankError::NoConvergence`] if the resulting factor exceeds the representable floating-point range.",
        "`qr_pivoted_permutation(a)`: 0-based column permutation vector `perm` from column-pivoted QR of `a`. Column-pivoted Householder QR (Businger and Golub). At each step the remaining column of largest norm is brought forward, so the diagonal of `R` decreases in magnitude and its decay reveals the numerical rank. Column norms are downdated and recomputed when cancellation makes the downdate unreliable. Each reflector applies to contiguous columns, with large independent column batches running in parallel. # Errors [`LowRankError::Shape`] for inconsistent storage or non-finite entries, and [`LowRankError::NoConvergence`] if the resulting factor exceeds the representable floating-point range.",
        "`qr_pivoted_rank(a, tol)`: numerical rank of matrix `a` from column-pivoted QR diagonal entries above `tol * max(|R_ii|)`. Column-pivoted Householder QR (Businger and Golub). At each step the remaining column of largest norm is brought forward, so the diagonal of `R` decreases in magnitude and its decay reveals the numerical rank. Column norms are downdated and recomputed when cancellation makes the downdate unreliable. Each reflector applies to contiguous columns, with large independent column batches running in parallel. # Errors [`LowRankError::Shape`] for inconsistent storage or non-finite entries, and [`LowRankError::NoConvergence`] if the resulting factor exceeds the representable floating-point range.",
        "`quadratic_residues(n)`: sorted list of nonzero quadratic residues modulo `n`.",
