        "`solve_pde(pde, u, ...)`: alias for `pdsolve`; solves `pde` for unknown `u`. Unified time-dependent PDE evolution driver supporting both fixed and adaptive step sizes via [`OdeStepMode`](crate::kernels::ode::OdeStepMode). `step_fn(t, state, dt)` advances `state` by a single step `dt` from time `t`. In [`OdeStepMode::Fixed`](crate::kernels::ode::OdeStepMode::Fixed), it takes uniform steps of size `dt` (with the final step landing on `t_span.1`). In [`OdeStepMode::Adaptive`](crate::kernels::ode::OdeStepMode::Adaptive), it delegates to [`adaptive_evolve`] with Richardson step-doubling of `order`. # Errors Returns [`FdmError::Domain`] for invalid time spans, step sizes, tolerances, non-finite states, or step-budget exhaustion.",
